---
import GuideLayout from "../../components/GuideLayout.astro";
import GuideRaceDemo from "../../components/GuideRaceDemo.astro";
---

<GuideLayout
  slug="race"
  description="Step three of the watershed build guide: add notes from two tabs at the same instant and confirm that both appear on the shared board."
>
  <div class="g-block">
    <h2>Add notes from both tabs at once</h2>
    <p>
      Open the board in two tabs. In each one, type a different note into{" "}
      <em>Went well</em> and click Add in both at the same moment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Both notes show up, in both tabs, in the same order. Nothing is lost.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="g-block">
    <h2>Each note uses a different key</h2>
    <p>
      Notes are keyed by note id in an <strong>OR-map</strong>, so two adds
      write two different keys — there's nothing for them to collide over.
    </p>
    <p>
      Store the board as a plain map keyed by column instead, and you'd get
      one note back, not two: a map with one key per column has one slot per
      column, so the second note overwrites the first — that's what
      “last write wins” means. Keying by note id means there's no shared slot
      to overwrite.
    </p>
  </div>

  <GuideRaceDemo notesOnly />
</GuideLayout>
